# OrderBy clause

The order by clause allows you puts results either asending (ASC) or descending (DESC) order. By default, without specifing ASC or DESC, ASC will be used. 

In AQL, the order by clause can be used with the following clauses: `WHERE` or `HAVING`. The order by clause combins with [binary operators](binaryop.md) and optionally [logic operators](logic.md).
The order by clause will work on all sources and field aliases; here we will show JSON source.

---

## Basic Syntax

```sql 
<order:star>
```
Or an individual field:

```sql
<order:single>
```

Only records matching the condition are returned.

## Common Table Expressions

```sql
<order:cte>
```